# Harsh Mentor, Immolation Shaman and Burning-Tree Shaman see an activation of an ability an effect grants as they see a printed
# one (CR 602.2, 613.1f): Deconstruction Hammer gives the equipped Ornithopter "{3}, {T}, Sacrifice Deconstruction Hammer:
# Destroy target artifact or enchantment", an ability of a creature on the battlefield that isn't a mana ability. On turn 3 Bot1's
# equip {1} (an ability of an artifact) triggers all three of Bot2's creatures: 2 + 1 + 1 = 4 damage, Bot1 at 16. Then the
# granted ability triggers all three again, above it on the stack (three items left after the first resolves, the Mox Sapphire
# still there): Bot1 at 12, and then Bot2's Mox Sapphire is destroyed. The Moxen tapped for mana trigger
# nothing (mana abilities are excluded, CR 605.1a, and the engine only records their activation).

